# Wasl data — all gitignored. Reference corpora are large, crawl snapshots are
# third-party page content we do not republish, and artifacts are regenerable.
# NOTE the leading **/. A pattern containing an internal slash is anchored to the
# repository root, so `data/cache/` matched /data/cache/ but NOT
# services/api/data/cache/ — which is where the cache actually landed, because
# WASL_DATA_DIR was resolved relative to the working directory.
#
# GitHub push protection caught the result: 304 cached third-party pages staged
# for commit, one containing another site's Mapbox token. Publishing crawl cache
# would also breach our own crawler policy, which says we do not republish
# substantial content from any site.
**/data/reference/
**/data/cache/
**/data/artifacts/
*.zip

# Eval output — regenerable; the README table is the committed artifact
services/api/eval/failures/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Generated during eval runs
**/data/artifacts/eval/

# Next.js local overrides
apps/web/.env.local
